
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Native firmware coverage (Clang/LLVM required, no board connected):

python3 -m unittest discover -s test/host -p 'test_*.py'
python3 test/host/run_coverage.py

The runner compiles seven test executables with ASan/UBSan and coverage enabled.
It reuses the installed ArduinoJson 6 headers from PlatformIO by default; supply
`--arduinojson /path/to/ArduinoJson/src` for a separate checkout. Set CXX,
LLVM_COV and LLVM_PROFDATA to select a matching Clang/LLVM toolchain on Linux.
On macOS, the runner uses clang++ and finds LLVM tools through xcrun.
The generated cpp-coverage.xml is imported by SonarCloud in CI. Its line coverage
includes actual production source/header paths only; tests, UART/RTOS mocks and
uninstrumented code are not credited. Other firmware paths remain uncovered.

readback_checks.cpp exercises the complete u-blox/Unicore readback implementations:
UART lock cleanup, stale input preservation, short writes, virtual timeouts,
wrong/corrupt responses, message length/content validation, Survey-In readback,
coordinates/datum/sigma validation, MODE and multiline UNILOGLIST parsing.
sample_checks.cpp checks RTK freshness across millis wraparound and validates
GGA orthometric height plus geoid separation, including units and bad values.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Host checks (run from geodetic/esp32, no device required):

c++ -std=c++17 -fsanitize=address,undefined -g -Itest/host -Iinclude \
  test/host/base_checks.cpp src/functions/gnss/gnss_cmd_builder.cpp \
  src/functions/gnss/ublox_commands.cpp src/functions/gnss/unicore_commands.cpp \
  -o /tmp/esp32-base-checks
/tmp/esp32-base-checks
python3 -B test/host/check_cors.py ../.. /tmp/esp32-base-checks
python3 -B test/host/check_gnss_stream.py
python3 -B test/host/check_rover_gga.py
python3 -B test/host/check_gga_position.py
python3 -B test/host/check_wifi_handover.py
python3 -B test/host/check_auto_base_location.py
python3 -B test/host/check_vn2000.py
c++ -std=c++17 -fsanitize=address,undefined -Itest/host -Iinclude \
  test/host/mqtt_write_checks.cpp -o /tmp/esp32-mqtt-checks
/tmp/esp32-mqtt-checks
c++ -std=c++17 -fsanitize=address,undefined -Itest/host -Iinclude \
  test/host/wifi_profiles_checks.cpp -o /tmp/esp32-wifi-checks
/tmp/esp32-wifi-checks

Shared codec and MQTT dispatch checks:

c++ -std=c++17 -DNATIVE_BUILD -fsanitize=address,undefined \
  -Itest/host -Iinclude test/host/codec_checks.cpp \
  src/functions/backend/Backend_Agent_Codec.cpp -o /tmp/esp32-codec-checks
/tmp/esp32-codec-checks
python3 -B test/host/check_mqtt_dispatch.py

wifi_profiles_checks.cpp validates credentials using Wifi_Credentials.h;
it does not restore the removed AP or multiple-network profile feature.
check_wifi_handover.py reads the current Network_Manager.cpp implementation.
check_status_flash.py requires a real flashed device and a closed Serial Monitor;
it observes startup logs and does not upload firmware. The PlatformIO tests
in init_preference and test_sim run on hardware, not as host checks.

VS Code uses PlatformIO-generated IntelliSense configuration. These host
files do not need to be added to the production compilation database.

u-blox configuration verification (no device required):

python3 -B test/host/check_ublox_verification.py
c++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined -Iinclude \
  test/host/config_verification_checks.cpp -o /tmp/esp32-config-verification
/tmp/esp32-config-verification

Upstream-cleanup regression checks (native C++, ASan/UBSan):
  python3 -B test/host/check_status_stream.py
  python3 -B test/host/check_websocket_frames.py
The optional first argument is a previous firmware root. Status JSON is compared
across versions; stream commands use expected outcomes because the old handler
contains dangling JSON keys. WebSocket checks run unchanged on either version.

NTRIP reconnect status and transition-only logging:
  python3 -B test/host/check_ntrip_reconnect.py

Workflow Base-mode restoration and CORS-to-UART delivery:
  python3 -B test/host/check_workflow_restore.py

Run `python3 geodetic/esp32/test/host/check_nvs_inventory.py` for real JSON field values, nested secret masking and pagination.
Run `python3 geodetic/esp32/test/host/check_wifi_nvs.py` for Wi-Fi NVS reuse and missing-key persistence.
Run `python3 geodetic/esp32/test/host/check_projection_audit.py` for fixed M3/M6 RTCM1025 packets in both decoders, raw evidence preservation and report memory/serialization.
Run `python3 geodetic/esp32/test/host/check_workflow_progress.py` for JSON key ownership and Vietnamese workflow reports under ASan/UBSan.
